Task 1: Check if EFI firmware exists on the system  
Description Task 1: Stat the /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ directory to determine if the system is EFI-based  

Task 2: Remove GRUB configuration file on EFI systems  
Description Task 2: Delete /boot/grub2/grub.cfg if the EFI firmware exists  

Task 3: Install custom user template for GRUB  
Description Task 3: Copy a template file named 01_users.j2 to /etc/grub.d/01_users with proper permissions  

Task 4: Add EFI password protection to GRUB  
Description Task 4: Insert a password_pbkdf2 line into /etc/grub2-efi.cfg for EFI systems  

Task 5: Add MBR password protection to GRUB  
Description Task 5: Insert a password_pbkdf2 line into /etc/grub2.cfg for MBR systems  

Task 6: Add unrestricted access to GRUB password entries  
Description Task 6: Modify GRUB password entries to include --unrestricted flag if enabled


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
   - name: Check if EFI firmware exists on the system
     stat:
       path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/
     register: efi_firmware

   - name: Remove GRUB configuration file on EFI systems
     file:
       path: /boot/grub2/grub.cfg
       state: absent
     when: efi_firmware.stat.isdir is defined and efi_firmware.stat.isdir

   - name: Install custom user template for GRUB
     copy:
       src: 01_users.j2
       dest: /etc/grub.d/01_users
       mode: '0755'

   - name: Add EFI password protection to GRUB
     blockinfile:
       path: /etc/grub2-efi.cfg
       insertafter: '^menuentry'
       block: |
         password_pbkdf2 [user] [hashed password]
     when: efi_firmware.stat.isdir is defined and efi_firmware.stat.isdir

   - name: Add MBR password protection to GRUB
     blockinfile:
       path: /etc/grub2.cfg
       insertafter: '^menuentry'
       block: |
         password_pbkdf2 [user] [hashed password]
     when: efi_firmware.stat.isdir is defined and not efi_firmware.stat.isdir

   - name: Add unrestricted access to GRUB password entries
     lineinfile:
       path: "{{ '/etc/grub2-efi.cfg' if efi_firmware.stat.isdir is defined and efi_firmware.stat.isdir else '/etc/grub2.cfg' }}"
       regexp: '^password_pbkdf2'
       line: 'password_pbkdf2 [user] [hashed password] --unrestricted'
       backrefs: yes
     when: enable_unrestricted_access | bool

   # Add a line break at the end of the file
   

